From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:33:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] build: gate non-WASI dependencies by target

Move dependencies that do not build for wasm32-wasip1 (cloud SDKs,
reqwest, rustls/rcgen with aws-lc, keyring, TUI, prompts, signal
handling, file locking, keepass, enpass, and since 1.40.0 the
Kubernetes client (kube, k8s-openapi) and the vendored Lua 5.4 of the
Lua plugin provider (mlua), which would need a C toolchain) under
cfg(not(target_os = "wasi")). On WASI, age is built with ssh only and
tokio with rt, macros, sync, time, io-util, fs and io-std. chrono's
serde feature is now requested directly instead of through
feature unification.

Native targets keep the same dependency set and features.

